     <h1 class="title" title="Gangtok Hill Station">Gangtok</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/east-india-hill-stations/gangtok-hill-station.gif" title="Gangtok hill station" alt="Gangtok hill station, hill stations in india, east india hill stations, Gangtok" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>

<b>Location:</b> Sikkim<br />
<b>Area:</b> 250 Square Km<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Unity in Diversity<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> September to October</p>     
<p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Kenchanchunga Mountains, East India Culture</p>
<p>The <b>capital of Sikkim</b>, is a unique mountain resort in northeast India and undoubtedly one of the most popular. Perched atop a hill at an altitude of 1700 meters, Gangtok is famous for its natural beauty and spectacular views of <b>Kanchenjunga</b>, the <b>world's highest mountain</b>. The city offers a temperate climate with temperatures around 23 degrees Celsius in summer and about 6 degrees Celsius in winter.</p>

